    <dashboard name='Takeaways'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='760' maxwidth='1100' minheight='760' minwidth='1100' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='104' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='100000' id='105' type-v2='text' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='24'>Takeaways</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>1.  Shopping centers have the strongest fundamentals: occupancy keeps rising and same-property NOI grows about 4% a year, faster than malls.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>2.  Malls are the cheapest and most indebted group, and the stocks bounced the most as investors came back to them.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>3.  Net-lease REITs are almost 100% leased but trade like bonds: a 1-point jump in the 10-year Treasury lined up with about a 16% drop in their quarterly return, vs. about 10% for shopping centers and malls.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>4.  Interest rates still drive a lot of the quarter-to-quarter stock moves for every group, so strong property results do not always show up in the stock right away.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#666666' fontsize='12'>Limits: 2023-2026 only; FFO and occupancy come from company press releases (checked against the text); a few of the newest quarters are not in the SEC data yet.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{22F9C518-BFAE-4B4C-97E6-C8100624AABE}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name='Title'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='760' maxwidth='1100' minheight='760' minwidth='1100' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='102' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='100000' id='103' type-v2='text' w='54166' x='0' y='0'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='22'>Retail REITs: Who Is Winning, and Does It Show Up in the Stock?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='15'>ISA 401 Final Project  |  Fall 2026  |  Section A  |  Team [#]</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='15'>Tyler Draeger  &amp;  Kenneth Kelly</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='16'>The question</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='13'>Among the 24 publicly traded U.S. retail REITs, are shopping center owners doing better than malls and net-lease REITs on occupancy and rent growth, and does that show up in stock returns and valuations, or do interest rates matter more?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='16'>Where the data comes from</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>- Nareit REIT directory (web scraping): list of REITs, returns, dividends</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>- SEC EDGAR (API): revenue, net income, assets, liabilities</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>- 370 earnings press releases (LLM extraction): occupancy, NOI growth, FFO</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>- FRED (API): 10-year Treasury  |  Yahoo Finance (API): stock prices</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#666666' fontsize='12'>Use the Property Type filter on each page to focus on one group. Hover over any mark for details.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='93333' id='101' name='REITs by Property Type' w='45834' x='54166' y='3333' />
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{369B90D4-F9A3-4873-9832-9AEACBA0FB3B}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
